          </div>
          <p>Leadership Development at SoESC fosters a Sewa-centered approach by building public leaders through immersive learning, capacity building, and system strengthening—creating a community of changemakers driving transformation.</p>
          <ul class="list">
            <li>Sewa-centered leadership approach is promoted within public systems through targeted interventions.</li>
            <li>The Piramal School of Leadership implements a 4-stack leadership model based on Sewa principles.</li>
            <li>A 24x7 omnichannel approach is used to reinforce behavioral change across all stakeholder levels, especially School Principals, Heads, and Middle Managers.</li>
            <li>Leaders are identified and nurtured to build a community of changemakers.</li>
            <li>State and District leaders are empowered through practice-led, actionable research.</li>
            <li>Workbooks are developed for district officials, and forums are created to share best practices across states.</li>
            <li>The interventions focus on strengthening State and District institutions by developing a pipeline of Sewa-focused leaders.</li>
            <li>Capacity-building efforts include improving service delivery, creating merit-based HR systems, and enabling learning through technology.</li>
            <li>The overall goal is to cultivate effective, service-oriented leadership within public education systems.</li>
